<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Determine a Solution to Inequalities</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00663</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Determine a Solution to Inequalities</md:title>
    <md:uuid>18b472e0-edfa-4e6b-8774-f01b981d9e3d</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">Is the ordered pair <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5.43</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> a solution to all, some, or none of these
        inequalities? Be prepared to explain your reasoning.</para>
      <list id="list-00001">
        <item><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></item>
        <item><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></item>
        <item><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mo>≥</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></item>
        <item><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mo>≥</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></item>
      </list>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
